WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
(dramatic music)

00:00:00.981 --> 00:00:01.814
(whip cracking)

00:00:01.814 --> 00:00:02.830
- [Narrator] Wushu is the modern term

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.053
in China for martial arts.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.943
It's especially beloved by
one wushu master in Macao.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.460
He has made it his life's mission

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.740
to pass on the ancient forms of combat

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.414
that captured his heart as a young boy.

00:00:17.414 --> 00:00:20.164
(dramatic music)

00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:27.406
(foreign language)

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:40.760
Today, Master Pun runs the Macao Lo Lung

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.660
Sport General Association,
founded in 1938.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.610
There are countless varieties of wushu.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.593
One of these styles is Choy Li Fut.

00:00:51.766 --> 00:00:54.683
(foreign language)

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.480
Other staples of wushu are the
dragon dance and lion dance,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.700
which require an enormous
amount of physical strength.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.083
More than 2,000 years old, they
are inseparable from wushu.

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:38.092
(foreign language)

